// Package fixtures holds the Go fixtures of the `stuttering-name-go` tool rule.
//
// This file holds one exported name of every shape revive reads as repetitive:
// a type and a function whose next rune after the package name opens a new
// word, and a type whose next rune is an underscore. The tool must report each
// one. A tool upgrade that stops reporting a shape makes the doctor mark the
// rule unusable.
package fixtures

// PlainRecord is a documented exported type that does not open with the
// package name, so only the names below are reported.
type PlainRecord struct{}

// FixturesRecord opens with the package name, so a caller outside the package
// writes `fixtures.FixturesRecord` and reads the word two times. The doc
// comment changes nothing: the check reads the NAME.
type FixturesRecord struct{}

// FixturesBuild carries the same repetition on a function.
func FixturesBuild() {}

// Fixtures_Thing carries the same repetition with an underscore where the two
// names above carry an upper-case rune. Either one opens a new word.
type Fixtures_Thing struct{}
